  "description": "MEJSUS crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C40 H48 La3 N8 O22 1+,2(C20 H22 La1 N4 O10 1-),10(H2 O1),Na1 1+. From the CIF bond table, La1 (La) has 6 O neighbors; La2 (La) has 6 O neighbors; La3 (La) has 6 O neighbors; La4 (La) has 6 O neighbors; La5 (La) has 6 O neighbors; La3A? (La) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 0.785-5.444 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 15.23-157.87°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [La(octapa)(H2O)2]2[La(H2O)6.15]0.5Na0.5 (C40H56.3La2.5N8Na0.5O26.15). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
